      "name": null,
      "problem": "${f}^{′}(x)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $[\\,8{x}^{3}+16x{y}^{2}-16x$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$]$",
      "worked_solution": "For our scalar function, we have that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={(∇f)}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEarlier, we found that \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=8{x}^{3}+16x{y}^{2}-16x.\n$$\n\nThe partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-8{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}-1)=16{x}^{2}y+12y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,8{x}^{3}+16x{y}^{2}-16x\\, & \\,16{x}^{2}y+12y\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
