    "q-168890": {
      "dom_id": "question-168890",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the second partial derivatives of $f.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y}=\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}",
      "worked_solution": "Previously, we found that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=8{x}^{3}+16x{y}^{2}-16x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=16{x}^{2}y+12y.\n$$\n\nComputing the second partial derivatives, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8{x}^{3}+16x{y}^{2}-16x)=24{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}-16 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(16{x}^{2}y+12y)=32xy \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(16{x}^{2}y+12y)=16{x}^{2}+12\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
